If a patient has an opioid-withdrawal-symptom then every clinician should consider a first-line-taper-slowing-option for the patient.
If a patient has an opioid-withdrawal-symptom then every clinician should consider a first-line-taper-pause-option for the patient.
If a patient has an opioid-withdrawal-symptom then a taper-slowing is first-line for the opioid-withdrawal-symptom.
If a patient has an opioid-withdrawal-symptom then a taper-pause is first-line for the opioid-withdrawal-symptom.
